\newpage
\begin{verbatim}

% RULE RpppConjsentVar
< m1: PREPPPROP{PREPPPROPrec1}[I1:mu1] 

  m2: T1
>

< m : PREPPPROP{PREPPPROPrec1}
            [ leftdislocrel/T1,
              I2:mu1
            ] 
>


   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: NOT EXIST(mu1, [leftdislocrel/..])
       I2: NOT EXIST(mu1, [I21:rel1/..])
         I21: rel1 IN [leftdislocrel, locadvrel, tempadvrel,
                       postsentadvrel]
      >

<
   SUBRULE (* 1. SENTENCE *)
      < T1: SENTENCEVAR{SENTENCEVARrec1} >
      < T1: SENTENCEVAR{SENTENCEVARrec1} >

      COMP
         <
          C1: SENTENCEVARrec1.adverbial = true AND
              SENTENCEVARrec1.temporal  = false
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: SENTENCEVARrec1.adverbial = true AND
              SENTENCEVARrec1.temporal  = false
          A1: @
         >

   SUBRULE (* 2. PREPP *)
      < T1: PREPPVAR{PREPPVARrec1} >
      < T1: PREPPVAR{PREPPVARrec1} >

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       T1: PREPPVARrec1.synppefs * [synNP, synOPENGERUND] <> []
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >
>
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RpppConjsentVar
\item[* relevant examples:] Although we don't live here yet, we are against 
foreigners in this neighbourhood; Without wanting to make you nervous, you are 
against what the boss proposed just yesterday
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] PreppPropFormation
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) RC\_PrepSentAdvVar
\item[* date of creation:] 7-MAR-1989 
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] RIdentConjsentVar
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 24/10/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
1) there is only one var-extraction order in analysis (i.e.\ tempadv - locadv - 
sentadv), correlated with the actual surface order of the vars (which is 
sentadv (momentarily only in leftdislocrel) - locadv - tempadv), so there is 
right to left extraction)\\
2) in generation, there are more orders possible for insertion (depending on 
source language)\\
3) the extraction order for elements of the same class remains the same over 
languages, with for locadvs and sentadv/conjsent obligatory left to right 
insertion 
(locadv1 - locadv2 - locadv3 etc) = right to left extraction, and for tempadvs 
(which have a different surface order in Dutch) the other way around.
Since there can be only one leftdislocrel, two sentadvs or a sentadv 
and a conjsent both in leftdislocrel cannot occur. Should this be wanted, an 
alternative position 
for sentadvs has to be decided using the attribute `position' of advs (That is 
not used yet). 
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:]
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) The condition 
on no other leftdislocrels orders this rule before the SentAdvVar rule
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
